  "id": "dystrophia-myotonica",
  "term": "dystrophia myotonica",
  "definition": "Dystrophia myotonica is a neuromuscular disorder marked by gradually worsening muscle wasting, myotonia, and other body-system atrophy. Mild intellectual disability can also occur, and forms of the disorder are associated with abnormal DNA repeat expansions in the DMPK gene or the zinc finger protein-9 gene.",
